{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "diffusers-nano-policy-droid",
      "prompt": "Roll out the Cosmos3 DROID policy once with the diffusers path on this machine's single GPU: nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Policy-DROID in bfloat16, guardrails disabled for this smoke, the notebook's default instruction \"Pick up the object and place it in the target container.\", conditioned on the cookbook's DROID LeRobot example (../cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/action/assets/droid_lerobot_example/, relative to this skill directory; its three camera clips are git-LFS objects, materialised as the skill documents, no substitute media). Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main) as COSMOS3_REPO. Put the notebook's outputs under outputs/ so that the rollout video is outputs/droid_policy/droid_policy.mp4 and the predicted action chunk is outputs/droid_policy/droid_policy_action.json, and record the verified frame count, fps and action shape in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "A 17-frame droid_policy.mp4 at 15 fps and a 16-step droid_policy_action.json produced by Cosmos3-Nano-Policy-DROID through Cosmos3OmniPipeline exist under outputs/droid_policy/, and result_summary.md records model, settings, runtime, peak CUDA memory and the verified shapes.",
      "assertions": [
        "The three DROID camera clips were materialised from the public repository's LFS objects (sizes and sha256 matching the pointers) and the 640x540 conditioning frame was composed from them, not from substitute media",
        "nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Policy-DROID was loaded in bfloat16 on the GPU through Cosmos3OmniPipeline from the dedicated diffusers venv and called with a CosmosActionCondition in policy mode (no raw_actions), as the skill documents",
        "outputs/droid_policy/droid_policy.mp4 is a valid 17-frame video at 15 fps and outputs/droid_policy/droid_policy_action.json holds a 16-step action chunk, both written by the pipeline run recorded in the transcript",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the video and the action JSON trace to a real pipeline run in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md reports the settings, wall-clock time, GPU memory and the verified frame count / action shape actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/droid_policy/droid_policy.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 20000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/droid_policy/droid_policy_action.json",
          "min_bytes": 300
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "materialise DROID clips",
        "env setup",
        "model load",
        "policy rollout",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vllm-omni-edge-policy-droid",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge-Policy-DROID with vLLM-Omni (guardrails disabled) and run ONE one-shot DROID policy rollout through its asynchronous /v1/videos API with the notebook's default instruction, conditioned on the cookbook's DROID LeRobot example (../cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/action/assets/droid_lerobot_example/, relative to this skill directory; its three camera clips are git-LFS objects, materialised as the skill documents, no substitute media). Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main) as the COSMOS3_REPO the server mounts. Put the notebook's outputs under outputs/ so that the [16, 8] action chunk is outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/action.json and the rollout video, when the server returns one, is outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/policy_rollout.mp4; then stop the server and record time-to-ready, request latency and the action shape in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "The vLLM-Omni server serves Cosmos3-Edge-Policy-DROID, one /v1/videos policy request completes, action.json with a finite [16, 8] chunk (and the rollout video when returned) exists under outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/, and result_summary.md records server command, time-to-ready and latency.",
      "assertions": [
        "The three DROID camera clips were materialised from the public repository's LFS objects and the 640x540 composite was built from them, not from substitute media",
        "The vLLM-Omni server was started with the notebook's documented image and flags for Cosmos3-Edge-Policy-DROID and /v1/models answered before the policy request was sent",
        "The request used the notebook's documented /v1/videos form and extra_params (action_mode policy, domain_name droid_lerobot, raw_action_dim 8, action_chunk_size 16) with the Edge structured JSON prompt",
        "outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/action.json holds a finite [16, 8] action chunk returned by the server, and the rollout video was saved when the content endpoint returned a body",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated, the server was stopped at the end, and result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, request latency and action shape actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/action.json",
          "min_bytes": 500
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "materialise DROID clips",
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "policy request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sglang-nano-policy-droid",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Policy-DROID with SGLang (guardrails disabled for this smoke) and run the notebook's two-request DROID policy flow with its default instruction: POST /v1/actions/generations for the [16, 8] action chunk, then the forward-dynamics POST /v1/videos rollout rendered from that chunk on the same server, conditioned on the cookbook's DROID LeRobot example (../cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/action/assets/droid_lerobot_example/, relative to this skill directory; its three camera clips are git-LFS objects, materialised as the skill documents, no substitute media). Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main) as COSMOS3_REPO. Put the notebook's outputs under outputs/ so that the action chunk is outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/action.json and the rollout video is outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/policy_rollout.mp4; then stop the server and record time-to-ready, both request latencies, the action shape and the rollout's frame count in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "An SGLang-served Cosmos3-Nano-Policy-DROID answers the /v1/actions/generations request with a finite [16, 8] chunk and the forward-dynamics /v1/videos job renders a 17-frame policy_rollout.mp4 from it; both files are under outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/ and result_summary.md records readiness, latencies and shapes.",
      "assertions": [
        "The three DROID camera clips were materialised from the public repository's LFS objects and the 640x540 composite was built from them, not from substitute media",
        "The SGLang server was started with the notebook's documented image and flags and /v1/models answered before the first request",
        "outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/action.json holds a finite [16, 8] chunk from /v1/actions/generations and outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/policy_rollout.mp4 is the 17-frame rollout the forward-dynamics /v1/videos job rendered from that chunk",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the action chunk and the rollout trace to real server responses in the transcript",
        "The server was stopped at the end and result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, both request latencies, the action shape and the rollout frame count actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/action.json",
          "min_bytes": 500
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/action_policy_droid/video_api/policy_rollout.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 10000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "materialise DROID clips",
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "policy request",
        "rollout request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "trt-edge-llm-edge-policy-droid",
      "prompt": "Run Cosmos3-Edge-Policy-DROID through TensorRT-Edge-LLM v0.11.0 on this x86 host with one H100, exactly as the skill documents: build the policy engines (und-prefill, gen, vae-encoder) with the direct builder from nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge-Policy-DROID, compose the 640x540 DROID concat_view observation from the cookbook's DROID LeRobot example (../cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/action/assets/droid_lerobot_example/, relative to this skill directory; its three camera clips are git-LFS objects, materialised as the skill documents, no substitute media), and run cosmos3_policy_inference with --viewPoint concat_view, the notebook's default instruction and its zero placeholder state; copy the resulting action.json to outputs/trt_edge_llm_action.json. The setup guide lists 'an x86 developer build' among the engine-build targets, so the whole notebook is in scope on this host; its C++ runtime build and the engine build are heavy, so make a genuine attempt at every step (upstream installation of v0.11.0, the runtime build with -DBUILD_EXPERIMENTAL_MODELS=ON and -DENABLE_CUTE_DSL=ALL, the engine build, the inference run). Only after a real attempt has failed, record the exact failing step, its command and error and the measured resource numbers in result_summary.md; never fabricate action.json.",
      "expected_outcome": "outputs/trt_edge_llm_action.json holds the action chunk cosmos3_policy_inference wrote from engines built with tensorrt-edgellm-build on this host; only if a step genuinely fails on this x86 host does result_summary.md instead document the exact blocker with measured numbers.",
      "assertions": [
        "TensorRT-Edge-LLM v0.11.0 was installed and built as the skill documents (builder extra plus the C++ runtime with -DBUILD_EXPERIMENTAL_MODELS=ON and -DENABLE_CUTE_DSL=ALL), or the install/build failure is documented with the exact command and error after a real attempt",
        "The policy engines were built with tensorrt-edgellm-build --components und-prefill,gen,vae-encoder from nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge-Policy-DROID and the notebook's contract check (content 640x540, attention_position_ids) passed, or the build failure is documented with evidence",
        "The 640x540 concat_view observation was composed from the three materialised DROID clips, not from substitute media",
        "outputs/trt_edge_llm_action.json is the action.json written by cosmos3_policy_inference ([batch, chunk, action_dimension]), or - only after a genuine attempt on this host - result_summary.md documents the concrete blocker with measured numbers",
        "No output was fabricated: any action.json present traces to a real cosmos3_policy_inference run in the transcript",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "materialise DROID clips",
        "runtime install and build",
        "engine build",
        "policy inference or blocker analysis",
        "summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN",
    "GITHUB_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 90,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
